cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "SCAX: Statistically Certified Abductive Explanations for Disease Classification"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Biswas
    given-names: Md Anas
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-0113-5816"
    affiliation: "School of Computing, University of Portsmouth"
  - family-names: Laila
    given-names: Alif
    affiliation: "School of Computing, University of Portsmouth"
repository-code: "https://github.com/anasbiswas1/scax-research"
abstract: >-
  SCAX is a certify-or-abstain framework for disease classification on public health data. A tree
  ensemble is trained; a logic solver proves explanations (boxes of feature ranges) inside which the
  model's prediction cannot change; each box receives a statistical certificate on how often the
  recorded outcome disagrees with the prediction among people inside it; and the release policy is
  certified on held-out data before deployment.
keywords:
  - formal explanations
  - abductive explanations
  - selective prediction
  - Clopper-Pearson
  - tree ensembles
  - BRFSS
